// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: read-modify-write on volatile global
// RMW-LAUNDER (2026-08-11), spawn sink. TSan-CONFIRMED data race on this exact
// program before the fix ("Read of size 4 ... Previous write of size 4 by
// thread T1", both inside bump).
//
// `volatile` exempts a global from the spawn race scan for the SINGLE-WORD flag
// idiom — one plain load or one plain store. A read-modify-write is neither.
// Axis A3 added a carve-out for exactly that, but matched only a compound
// assign whose target is a NAMED global, so moving the `+= 1` one hop behind a
// pointer parameter made the program compile. `counter += 1` written directly
// in `worker` is rejected; this was not.
volatile u32 counter;

void bump(volatile *u32 p) { *p += 1; }
void worker() { bump(&counter); }

u32 main() { spawn worker(); u32 x = counter; return x & 1; }
